{
 "_doc": "The extra companions of the KotOR 2 world (slots 12 to 31). Ids only: table rows and class ids, no game text. Every extra is built from ONE generic creature template, 'base' (a vetted companion body: it equips, unequips, levels up and saves like a companion), with the name, class, sex, portrait and look from here; the character's own leftover template is never used. 'look_method' says how the look reaches the game: 'disguise' (the template keeps its body and a permanent disguise effect with the look's appearance.2da row is applied by the dispatcher's tick, ap_look_<slot> in the seed) or 'template' (the row is written into the template's Appearance_Type). 'k1' characters are the KotOR 1 companions: their K2 appearance and portrait rows already exist (appearance 4-10, portraits 14, 33-39) and name models that are only missing from the files, so the player's own KotOR 1 install supplies them (tools/build_extra_assets.py); without it they use the generic fallback look and a player-head portrait of the same sex. 'k2' characters are story characters whose look is their own appearance row. 'ap' companions are generated: a look drawn from 'ap_looks' (none of the story companions' looks), a portrait drawn from 'portraits' by sex. 'armor' says whether the look's model shows armour (appearance modeltype B); gear can be equipped on every look either way. 'class' is the base class of the level-1 shell the rebuild raises to the player's level.",
